            "review_text": "Azalea\n2 contributions\n2\nGood food but were spiked with a cigarette by one of the workers\nOct 2019 • Friends\nAll was well and the food was delicious but be warned!! After eating our meal a man who worked there offered us a cigarette, my friend and I didn’t think much of it and accepted it. After 2 puffs of it I felt extremely ill straight away. My friend had smoked it before me and she went pale straight away. We knew we were in some type of danger so we left straight away trying to get to a safe place. I was immediately going in and out of consciousness, sweating extremely and could see my heart beating out of my chest. We were terrified, alone in Hanoi with no where to go and no one to help us. I started hallucinating and blacking out, all the while walking to our old Airbnb to try to find a room we could rest in and feel safe. My friend started loosing consciousness and vomiting. Sweating tremendously now and both our heart rates were beating extremely fast. We eventually after an hour of sitting in an alley got ourselves up, still very out of it and got to a hotel. After 3 hours of shaking, vomiting and sweating it slowly went away.... I don’t know if this is some kind of sick joke or if he was intentionally trying to drug us. I have heard horror stories of people in Vietnam and south east Asia being spiked with scopamine and loosing consciousness for a few days. I was fully aware what was happening As I was trying my best to figure out a safe place to go, as my friend was much worse then me. \nI’m horrified at what happened and I warn anyone out there, be very careful of what you are given, wether it be cigarettes or drinks or anything \nOur experience in Vietnam has been beautiful, up to this point I have never been so scared in my life \nThankyou kaoya hotpot, Hanoi for doing this too us \nIt really put the icing on the cake !\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 12, 2019",
